{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help","id":155041,"title":"Totem Creation Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-31T11:47:42-07:00","id":155041,"title":"Totem Creation Help","content":"So we come to time in our Sweden <b>Werewolf</b> game that players will hunt for they totem spirit. Players are agreed on some kind of Bear spirit, but can't decide on specific name/description. Can anyone help us with decision? How to find more on &quot;titles&quot; the totems can have? Like that in corebook example there is &quot;Mother Bear of Great Rivers&quot; - where can be found more ideas on those? Any sourcebooks references beside <b>Forsaken</b> corebook? Any good net links?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T19:52:18-07:00","id":155381,"title":"","content":"Well remember it just has to look like a bear. It can be anything in between. Perhaps a spirit of the hunt, or of natures wrath. Give it a name like springs-return for a rejuvenation minded spirit. I'm not to good with names myself, but keep those parameters in mind. You don't have to name it -bear of.........- try forming the stats your players want out of it first, THEN focus on the name. It might just come to you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T19:56:23-07:00","id":155383,"title":"","content":"What's the pack's theme? The Totem is gonna literally be the spirit of the pack. Take a moment to let that sink in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T21:25:17-07:00","id":155425,"title":"","content":"The Wolf-Blooded pack theme is problem. We have diverse cjaracters, binded only by &quot;we are hunting Malejin workers&quot; ( even if characters thinks of them for now as &quot;Satanic cult&quot; ) and that they were found by one old She-Wolf. In group there are: ( They all are new Wolf-Blooded, so a lesser werewolves )<br /> <br /> <b>Olaf</b> - large lumberjack, prone to acts of swith justice and ruthless. He he will probably end as Rahu.<br /> <b>Manfred</b> - anthropologist from big city, but the loves solitude of mountains. He is patient, but ants to bend the rules for himself. He is Ithaeur.<br /> <b>Aj\u00f6n</b> - young businessman, resolute, but prone to the impulsive outbursts. He is Irraka.<br /> <b>Vilhelm</b> - local hunter that was a disgraced after unwitting meeting with now Uratha mentor few years ago. He will probably be a Cathalith.<br /> <b>Elsa</b> - hesitant sociology student, that has great burning for justice for death of her childhood friend, and now to take the cult from the town. She is now Elodoth.<br /> <br /> Very diverse characters, connected with the idea of protecting or cleansing the town from the &quot;devils influence&quot;. Maybe Bear Spirit connected with Cleansing or Protection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-01-2014, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T22:57:19-07:00","id":155478,"title":"","content":"The-Fire-Stomper, maybe? A Bear Spirit who may see the Maeljin corruption as a potential fire which needs to be stepped on before it grows out of control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T23:17:09-07:00","id":155498,"title":"","content":"Was Smokey the Bear a thing outside of America? How about Yogi? A bear of harmless harassment, stealing pic-a-nic baskets and scaring campers in their tents or cars may be upset at the harsher antics of local bale hounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear#Myth_and_legend\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/Ours_brun_parcanimalierpyrenees_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear#Myth_and_legend\" target=\"_blank\"> Bear - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear#Myth_and_legend\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear#Myth_and_legend </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_in_heraldry\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Shield_and_Coat_of_Arms_of_Madrid_City_%281544-c.1600%29.svg/1280px-Shield_and_Coat_of_Arms_of_Madrid_City_%281544-c.1600%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_in_heraldry\" target=\"_blank\"> Bear in heraldry - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_in_heraldry\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_in_heraldry </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ursa_minor#History_and_mythology\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ursa_mi..._and_mythology</a> (star bears are cool)<br /> <br /> If it's just a flat out bear spirit, the spirit would probably look like a bear, if a bit more bearer than the average bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-01-2014, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T23:32:40-07:00","id":155509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=155478#post155478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The-Fire-Stomper, maybe? A Bear Spirit who may see the Maeljin corruption as a potential fire which needs to be stepped on before it grows out of control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Idea is interesting, but fires are very uncommon in Swedish Lapland were game takes place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b Players are caught in small valley near <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarek_National_Park\" target=\"_blank\">Sarek National Park</a> and they need to fight with Malejin serving pack of the territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=155498#post155498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was Smokey the Bear a thing outside of America?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so - in Poland we didn't heard of it, and so would I assume in deep Lapland. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=155498#post155498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Yogi? A bear of harmless harassment, stealing pic-a-nic baskets and scaring campers in their tents or cars may be upset at the harsher antics of local bale hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I know Yogi from 70s American cartoon that was aired in Poland from 90s - but I wouldn't put it as alien minded spirit guardian in horror game, to be sure. Maybe I'm weird, but I always envisoned Shadow Realm as mixture of <i>Princess Mononoke</i> with <i>Silent Hill</i>. More &quot;Great Bear of Longest Forest&quot; than &quot;Yogi the Picknic Stealer&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=155498#post155498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear#Myth_and_legend\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/Ours_brun_parcanimalierpyrenees_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear#Myth_and_legend\" target=\"_blank\"> Bear - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear#Myth_and_legend\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear#Myth_and_legend </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_in_heraldry\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Shield_and_Coat_of_Arms_of_Madrid_City_%281544-c.1600%29.svg/1280px-Shield_and_Coat_of_Arms_of_Madrid_City_%281544-c.1600%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_in_heraldry\" target=\"_blank\"> Bear in heraldry - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_in_heraldry\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_in_heraldry </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ursa_minor#History_and_mythology\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ursa_mi..._and_mythology</a> (star bears are cool)<br /> <br /> If it's just a flat out bear spirit, the spirit would probably look like a bear, if a bit more bearer than the average bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for links, maybe I will come with something from them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Wikipedia says that in Sarek Park often are classical <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_bear\" target=\"_blank\">Brown Bears</a>, so at least we have totem's &quot;skin&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-01-2014, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T23:44:44-07:00","id":155519,"title":"","content":"Yeah, some animal study site said there's around 1300 tracked bears in Sweden, too. Most of the spirit animal sites for bears (there's a lot) suggest pretty much the same things as the wikipedia bear entry under mythology.<br /> <br /> That said, it doesn't have to be a bear of honor or whatever, a bear spirit on its own isn't anything to shrug at. The Rockies hunting ground book has a big rocky spire with gouges in it that are legended to be from a great bear. Naturally there is also a great bear spirit, who acted as totem to many packs before Europeans came to America (it's a particularly powerful being). After that it lose a lot of power and went into hibernation, only to reawaken somewhat recently (for mysterious reasons that may be involved with a terrorist attack or a particularly close orbit of Mars to Earth). So far it's been standoffish, summoning bear spirits to guard its cave and mauling interlopers. There's a lot of plot hooks suggested with this.<br /> <br /> But you can probably make up some local legend or myth, or perhaps an old noble who used the bear as their standard and was particularly noble when protecting the area. Perhaps he was a religious man (and spirits that were spawned from it would have similar bents). It wouldn't have to be a particularly old legend.<br /> <br /> And it wasn't as much about Yogi as bears being notorious pests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-01-2014, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T00:06:03-07:00","id":155528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=155478#post155478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The-Fire-Stomper, maybe? A Bear Spirit who may see the Maeljin corruption as a potential fire which needs to be stepped on before it grows out of control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rolls-Over-Rousing-Coals, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T00:18:58-07:00","id":155534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=155519#post155519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, some animal study site said there's around 1300 tracked bears in Sweden, too. Most of the spirit animal sites for bears (there's a lot) suggest pretty much the same things as the wikipedia bear entry under mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume with that powerfull bears population, it's spirit guardian would have &quot;protection&quot; on them, even by having at least one dot in Influnace on Bears. He IS - literally - worshiped by bears of territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=155519#post155519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can probably make up some local legend or myth, or perhaps an old noble who used the bear as their standard and was particularly noble when protecting the area. Perhaps he was a religious man (and spirits that were spawned from it would have similar bents). It wouldn't have to be a particularly old legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going with old Sami tribe's myth, even if Uratha of region are having they creation myth based more on Nordic interpretation, with Vanir and Asir. Here are interesting info on <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sami_shamanism\" target=\"_blank\">Sami people shamanism belifes</a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T01:52:35-07:00","id":155557,"title":"","content":"Sami are interesting. I find the Nordics and protonorse/earlier germanics interesting too though. The Goths were bad ass kicking Romes ass. Could always make it a spirit of war, with a declaration against the maeljin. It'd be doubly fun if one of your players is a bale hound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T02:03:35-07:00","id":155560,"title":"","content":"There is very interesting mini-article on Wikipedia age of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_worship#Finns\" target=\"_blank\">Bear Worship about Finns</a> ( and Sumi people ) belifes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The bear was an important cult animal in </span></span></span><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnish_paganism\" target=\"_blank\">Finnish paganism</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. <b>The pre-Christian </b></span></span></span><b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnish_people\" target=\"_blank\">Finns</a></b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b> believed the bear to have come from the stars and that it had the ability to reincarnate.</b> After a successful </span></span></span><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Bear_hunt&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" target=\"_blank\">bear hunt</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, a celebration called </span></span></span><i>karhunpeijaiset</i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (literally &quot;celebration of the bear&quot;) was arranged in honour of the slain bear. The purpose of the ceremony was to placate the bear and to convince its soul that it was greatly respected by the people. The bear was so feared that some of the songs sung during the ceremony were meant to convince the bear it hadn't been slain by the hunters, rather that it had killed itself by accident. The people presiding over the ceremony tried to make the bear's soul happy so that the bear would want to reincarnate back into the forest. After the </span></span></span><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_meat\" target=\"_blank\">bear's meat</a> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">was eaten, the bones were buried. The skull, however, which was believed to contain the bear's soul, was placed high upon the branches of an old pine tree. This tree, </span></span></span><i>kallohonka</i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (skull pine), was probably a symbol of the world tree and the ceremony was meant to deliver the bear's soul back to the heavens, from where it had originated. From the heavens, the bear would come back and reincarnate to walk the earth.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Bears were not typically featured in early <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petroglyphs\" target=\"_blank\">petroglyphs</a>, like other animals such as the elk. It has been suggested that the bear was such a holy animal that it was forbidden to depict it. Moreover, it was forbidden to use the word for bear in casual conversation, so many euphemisms were developed. In fact, the current standard term for bear, <i>karhu</i>, is originally a euphemism (from <i>karhea</i> &quot;rough&quot;, referring to the rough fur). The oldest known and possibly the original name is <i>oksi</i>, preserved in many place names. The euphemisms were used because it was believed the bear would appear if its real name was called. Modern Finnish still contains many euphemisms for the bear. A similar thinking is behind the euphemisms for <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolf\" target=\"_blank\">wolf</a> (<i>susi</i>), such as <i>hukka</i> (&quot;loss&quot;).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>And this interpretaion from <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_carvings_at_Alta#Bears\" target=\"_blank\">rock cravings at Alta</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Of special interest are the tracks coming out of bear dens: they are often shown with tracks leading vertically through the carved image and crossing the horizontal tracks of other animals. <b>This has led some researchers to speculate that bears might have been in some way connected with a cult of the </b></span></span></span><b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afterlife\" target=\"_blank\">afterlife</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (or </span></span></span><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death\" target=\"_blank\">death</a></b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b> in general)</b> since the vertical tracks seem to indicate an ability of bears to pass between different layers of the world. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>With those bolded quotes logical maybe the cult of Bear Spirit From Stars, that would make sure the souls ( off all living things) will go to the underworld and the balance will preserved. He deals with the spiritual purity of the area because it violates the holy cycle which he guards. He is partly related to the spirit which puts out fires, because for him the effect Malejinn pollutes the world and it's delicate balance. I think that would give him Influences as Light (because it is the spirit of the stars) and Death (because it takes the dead to the other side). What do you think? You can a good name for such a spirit? And would he have influence on our material bears?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Found even cool graphics for Stellar Bear spirit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fc04.deviantart.net/fs36/i/2008/286/c/e/URSA_MAJOR_V2_by_myargie22.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://th03.deviantart.net/fs14/PRE/f/2007/107/8/1/Spirit_of_the_North_by_Kokiru.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-01-2014, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T02:33:52-07:00","id":156329,"title":"","content":"Totem Creation Process question - <b>could Pack buy new Totem Influences dots?</b> Even if not by the books, I would make it as house rule - but how much should it cost in Totem Points?<br /> <br /> I ask about it as logical is that this &quot;Star Bear for Dead&quot; Totem would have Influences like Light 2, Death 1, Bear 1, or even Light 2, Death 2, Bear 1, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T03:54:58-07:00","id":156368,"title":"","content":"There is no houserule necessary to do this. Under the original rules, spirits can buy the Greater Influence Numen (Book of Spirits, p. 142), which grants the spirit one extra dot in influences, as long as the influence does not exceed the spirits rank. Under GMC rules, spirits can exchange Numina for extra dots in influences, which is essentially the same. An extra numen costs three Totem Points, so a dot in an influence also costs this much.<br /> <br /> If you want to add that many influences or Numina to the Totem, you could think about granting it the Ban of Power Numen (Book of Spirits, p. 138). This lets the Totem take on an additional ban (or possibly bane, under GMC rules) that is more punitive than the spirit's default ban and gains the Totem two extra Numina, for a net increase of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T08:44:16-07:00","id":156555,"title":"","content":"Thanks <b>Penta</b>, very useful advises! I now think about our next game session &quot;Getting Totem Story&quot;.<br /> <br /> As it's centuries not worshiped spirit for departure of dead, I was thinking in putting him in dormant sleep inside a Barren that looks a lot like Elephants Graveyard form <i>Lion King, </i>with bears, and rarer human or other animals remains. He get's once in a while honor from one of dying bears remembering him that come to this place to be taken by him to stars. Even I thought he could be placed in Place-That-Isn't connected with this Barren, that is his &quot;room in sky&quot; high on this. PCs will need to awaken the sleeping bear spirit and bind or convince to they service. Does this idea looks as good for Totem hunting? What would be good &quot;hook&quot; for this kind of being to take Totem Oath? Maybe some interesting Bans - like &quot;All Must Dies Under The Stars&quot;? For any help I will be grateful. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20100522175615/lionking/images/b/b2/ElephantGraveyard2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:04:37-07:00","id":157906,"title":"","content":"I made the first draft of Light-of-Dead and it comes to 32 points cost. As I understand, taking more severe Ban will lower a cost so Severity Five Ban: &quot;<i>All Must Die Under Light of Stars</i>&quot; will take 25 points from this, yes? Because I think players will want to spend couple more Totem Points to get better bonuses. Am I correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:11:09-07:00","id":157915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=157906#post157906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made the first draft of Light-of-Dead and it comes to 32 points cost. As I understand, taking more severe Ban will lower a cost so Severity Five Ban: &quot;<i>All Must Die Under Light of Stars</i>&quot; will take 25 points from this, yes? Because I think players will want to spend couple more Totem Points to get better bonuses. Am I correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not correct. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At 32 Points the Ban for the Pack is already a Rank 5 Ban. And would require a Pack of 7 (assuming you do not allow them to go above 5 dots each) to invest 32 Dots of Totem between them (good thing they are only 3 Points/Dot). You cannot take a more sever Ban than a Rank 5 to reduce the cost at that point.<br /> <br /> You CAN take additional Spirit Bans (which applies only to the Spirit and not the Pack) to gain more power for the Spirit, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-03-2014, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:18:20-07:00","id":157923,"title":"","content":"Stellar-Flames-The-Night.<br /> Death, Stars, Light, Fire. Something larger than life and a hatred for the Maeljin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T12:12:43-07:00","id":158098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=157915#post157915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And would require a Pack of 7 (assuming you do not allow them to go above 5 dots each) to invest 32 Dots of Totem between them (good thing they are only 3 Points/Dot).</div> </div> </div> </div>So each Merit Dot buyed is 3 Totem Points? Like 10 Merit Points is 30 Totem Points? I'm confused... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=157915#post157915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You CAN take additional Spirit Bans (which applies only to the Spirit and not the Pack) to gain more power for the Spirit, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I could take Extra Ban, and get 6 points back from Numina, yes? What would you advise for this Stellar Death Bear spirit?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T13:30:10-07:00","id":158216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=158098#post158098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So each Merit Dot buyed is 3 Totem Points? Like 10 Merit Points is 30 Totem Points? I'm confused... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> So I could take Extra Ban, and get 6 points back from Numina, yes? What would you advise for this Stellar Death Bear spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each dot of Totem costs only 3 XP. No Incremental Costs for Totem.<br /> The Extra Ban is a Numen, as described below...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Bold\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Bold\"><b>Ban of Power: </b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">By taking on an additional ban, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">spirits can increase their power. Each additional ban </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">can give the spirit one of these awards: two Numina (a </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">net increase of one), one Willpower or an increase of </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">two maximum Essence. A spirit may take up to three </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">additional bans, but they may only have one particular </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">award. Each additional ban, including the first, must </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">be more punitive than the spirit\u2019s default ban</span>.</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-03-2014, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T15:53:03-07:00","id":158358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=157915#post157915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are not correct. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At 32 Points the Ban for the Pack is already a Rank 5 Ban. And would require a Pack of 7 (assuming you do not allow them to go above 5 dots each) to invest 32 Dots of Totem between them (good thing they are only 3 Points/Dot). You cannot take a more sever Ban than a Rank 5 to reduce the cost at that point.<br /> <br /> You CAN take additional Spirit Bans (which applies only to the Spirit and not the Pack) to gain more power for the Spirit, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, you can have 12 totem points in a single character. Or 25 all by yourself. Check out several NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T21:46:59-07:00","id":158699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=158358#post158358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, you can have 12 totem points in a single character. Or 25 all by yourself. Check out several NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? Totem is Merit, isn't it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T22:33:15-07:00","id":158733,"title":"","content":"There was no set limit to the amount of XP you could spend on the merit, a statement supported by several sample characters we saw in various books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T23:04:32-07:00","id":158751,"title":"","content":"Let's say I'm more inclined to limit Merits to only 5 dots, in most cases. That means that my 5 Wolves Pack can't buy 32 point Totem? If yes, what can be done to lower his cost so he could be buy-able?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T02:10:06-07:00","id":158843,"title":"","content":"Is a matter of simple math, if you force yourself to limit Merit dots to 5, then a 5 werewolves pack can at most habe a 25 dots Totem. But since it is you who are auto-limiting yourself, the best way to get your pack to get a 32 point Totem is simply use RAW. Sorry, but asking to solve a problem you are creating on purpose is a bit weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T02:15:03-07:00","id":158847,"title":"","content":"The thing is that the max on 25 points is merely for boons and the related ban. If you choose to spend the totem points in the totem's traits (power, finesse, new numina, etc) they are spent like as it was the totem's XP and it doesn't builds towards the ban.<br /> <br /> There is also examples in the book with totems costing over 30 dots, which have negligible bans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T03:00:10-07:00","id":158864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=158847#post158847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that the max on 25 points is merely for boons and the related ban. If you choose to spend the totem points in the totem's traits (power, finesse, new numina, etc) they are spent like as it was the totem's XP and it doesn't builds towards the ban.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is EXACTLY my case - Totem gives only about 11 points from bonuses for Pack. Rest are it's Traits and Numina, about 21 points. How to solve this, so Pack would be able to buy it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=158847#post158847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also examples in the book with totems costing over 30 dots, which have negligible bans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would love to see them and compare with mine, if you point me to them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:06:13-07:00","id":159051,"title":"","content":"The ban only counts the totem points spent on pack boons. The points used on the totem's trait don't count there, so you'd have a rank 3 ban with 11 points. Would cost 6 if you take a rank 5 ban, which gives you 5 more totem points to put on the spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:09:29-07:00","id":159059,"title":"","content":"<b>Raven-That-Sees-All</b><br /> <i>The carrion bird looks very healthy for one of her kind, with <br /> her feathers smooth and her eyes a glossy blue-black. She sees <br /> all that transpired below in the city\u2019s Shadow, and knows many <br /> secrets. Her shrieking caw is a warning to lesser spirits below that <br /> she is watching, though she mostly observes all in silent flight. </i><br /> Raven-That-Sees-All will join a pack only if they can <br /> tell her three secrets in the surrounding Shadow that she <br /> does not already know. The totem costs <b>32 points</b>.<br /> Attributes:Power 3, Finesse 3, Resistance 3<br /> Willpower:6<br /> Essence:15<br /> Initiative:6<br /> Speed:9<br /> Defense: 3 <br /> Corpus:5<br /> Influences:Secrets 2<br /> Numina:Chorus; Material Vision<br /> Bonuses:Wits 1 (given); 8 Essence Pool; Gift: Know <br /> Name (given) <br /> Ban: A pack sworn to Raven-That-Sees-All must <br /> take the eyes from every enemy the packmembers slay in <br /> the physical realm and leave the eyes at the locus for the <br /> totem to eat. This is difficult and dangerous if local law <br /> enforcement begins to notice a pattern to eyeless bodies, <br /> and if the ban is broken, the totem withdraws her favor and <br /> bonuses for an entire lunar cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:07:43-07:00","id":159121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=159051#post159051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ban only counts the totem points spent on pack boons. The points used on the totem's trait don't count there, so you'd have a rank 3 ban with 11 points. Would cost 6 if you take a rank 5 ban, which gives you 5 more totem points to put on the spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, as I got idea for Rank 5 Ban, and Totem would lov to get more in stats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As I understand, players buy Totems traits and Totems Ban determine sum on Pack Bonuses they get, correct? So If Totem has spend on traits 25 points, and have Pack Bonuses for 12 points. On points the players buy them from the Merits, and on Pack Bonuses are baught with spirits Ban Rank, yes?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:18:27-07:00","id":159131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=158358#post158358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, you can have 12 totem points in a single character. Or 25 all by yourself. Check out several NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only when allowed. I know what the books suggest, but I have been in some games where that was not allowed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:05:56-07:00","id":159168,"title":"","content":"No, first you figure out how much you're gonna spend in the boons, then figure out the ban, and take off totem points assuming you upgrade it, then pay the boons with the discount of a ban upgrade and finally add the rest of the dots into the totem's traits.<br /> <br /> So, if you have 25 points, 11 go towards the ban. But you upgrade it from rank 3 to five. That diminishes the cost by five point, the new ban (if you had upgraded it to four it would have been four points, etc). So, the boons would cost 6 points. After that you have 19 points to put on the totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:07:04-07:00","id":159171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=159131#post159131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only when allowed. I know what the books suggest, but I have been in some games where that was not allowed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's effectively a house-rule. Bears no actual matter when discussing the rules as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:22:28-07:00","id":159187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=159168#post159168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if you have 25 points, 11 go towards the ban. But you upgrade it from rank 3 to five. That diminishes the cost by five point, the new ban (if you had upgraded it to four it would have been four points, etc). So, the boons would cost 6 points. After that you have 19 points to put on the totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what if I got 21 point in Totem's traits, 11 in Pack Bonuses, 32 points in total?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:26:49-07:00","id":159190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=159187#post159187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what if I got 21 point in Totem's traits, 11 in Pack Bonuses, 32 points in total?</div> </div> </div> </div>You purchase the boons worth 11 points for 6; add the 5 you saved with the ban to the rest. 21-6=15.<br /> <br /> You don't magically get the points spent in boons back to add them to your totem. Check out the corebook's rules on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:39:11-07:00","id":159196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=159171#post159171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's effectively a house-rule. <b>Bears no actual matter when discussing the rules as written</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey! I resent that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">((I'm shite at remembering the rules, anyway, carry on.....))</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T13:20:17-07:00","id":159312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=159171#post159171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's effectively a house-rule. Bears no actual matter when discussing the rules as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned that in the original post you referred to, if you had paid any attention to it. *shrug*<br /> Not everyone allows a character to exceed the Merit Dots limit of 5 (unless Power Stat exceeds 5), after all. That is not an ambiguous rule, nor does it get explicitly contradicted in the Werewolf book, to my knowledge. Your statement to the contrary is simply an extrapolation based upon a bit of evidence, and nothing more. It is NOT a rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-04-2014, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T19:56:34-07:00","id":159664,"title":"","content":"Merit reads, literally:<br /> <br /> TOTEM (VARIES; SPECIAL)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T10:17:56-07:00","id":160050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=159664#post159664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merit reads, literally:<br /> <br /> TOTEM (VARIES; SPECIAL)</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it does - And then says absolutely NOTHING about what makes it SPECIAL except that it costs 3 points per dot (You know, outside the normal range of cost for a Merit - Seems pretty special to me; especially since the cost is not even listed in the Merit itself. You have to go to a table (page 66) to find that particular tidbit out. An issue that Continues to crop up, as witnessed above). THAT is special enough to be the complete and total necessary addendum. Get off the high horse there. I already mentioned (IN THE FIRST POST I MADE) that you could go over the 5 dot limit if the table allowed it. NOT ALL TABLES ALLOW THAT. *sheesh*<br /> <br /> SO... here is the text of the Totem Merit (from page 79 of the WTF Book)...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Werewolves lead a uniquely dangerous existence. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">They are closely tied to the spirit world and must </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">frequently face dangers that human beings cannot conceive. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">To help deal with these obstacles, Uratha forge </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">pacts with various spirits for mutual aid and assistance. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Many packs take this practice to the next level, binding </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">a spirit to their pack to serve as a patron \u2014 their pack </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">totem. A pack\u2019s relationship with its totem is something </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">like a compact between wartime allies. The totem looks </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">after the pack, and the pack works to aid and honor the </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">totem in a relationship as old as the world itself. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">This Merit is shared by all members of the pack; </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">each member who contributes Merit points to Totem </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">reaps the benefits, and the totem becomes stronger. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Dots placed in this Merit are spent on the pack totem, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">increasing its power in a number of ways.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">The other thing that makes the Merit: Totem SPECIAL is that the Pack members share their dots in Totem (they ADD them together) to get a total dot expenditure to create their Totem. Tell me... WHERE DOES IT SAY that I can abrogate the 5-Dot limits of Merits?<br /> <br /> Oh, wait - Nowhere does it actually SAY that (that I can find - and it is possible that I have missed it all these years). You extrapolate that from a few examples. THAT is all you did. You cannot point to an actual rule that allows that, can you?<br /> <br /> Whether it is RAI or not is irrelevant, it is not RAW as far as I can tell. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-05-2014, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T13:19:19-07:00","id":160183,"title":"","content":"If it was limited to five dots each, it would say<br /> <br /> TOTEM (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> I rest my case. Quit nitpicking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T06:54:08-07:00","id":160762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=160183#post160183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was limited to five dots each, it would say<br /> <br /> TOTEM (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> I rest my case. Quit nitpicking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Says the Nitpicker. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> You should not rest on your laurels, you may get boils.<br /> <br /> To the topic...<br /> <br /> I never said it was only limited to 5 (though you keep trying to pin that on me, you would be wrong). However, nowhere does it say that you EXPLICITELY exceed the 5 Dot limit before your Power stat goes above 5 (which is the general rule for stats of any type above 5). Many Merits cannot go above 5, no matter the Level of your powerstat. Totem can obviously do so. To exceed such limits by RAW, however, you need a higher powerstat than 5. So, therefore, not everyone will allow such expenditures until such a time as you exceed 5 on your powerstat. And that is RAW (because nowhere in Werewolf is that explicitly countered). What you are touting is most likely RAI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-06-2014, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T07:04:22-07:00","id":160767,"title":"","content":"I know skills and attributes need power stat increases to get above 5 (outside of certain cases, like vampire physical disciplines and werewolf shapechanging and others), but where does it ever say merits do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2014, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T07:17:38-07:00","id":160777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=160767#post160767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know skills and attributes need power stat increases to get above 5 (outside of certain cases, like vampire physical disciplines and werewolf shapechanging and others), but where does it ever say merits do?</div> </div> </div> </div>General rule, no ability may exceed 5 without a powerstat above 5. Reinforced by Vampire and Resources (a Normal 1-5 Merit). In Vampire's case, it explicitly can provide additional dots above 5 when your BP goes above 5. And again, back to what I said all along. Some tables will allow the Totem Merit to exceed 5 naturally, and others will only allow such things when Primal Urge exceeds 5. That was my original statement, and it is not wrong, because there is precedence in the actual rules (RAW not RAI) to back that up. Appealing to sample characters is an extrapolation, not a rule. *shakes head*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T07:38:01-07:00","id":160786,"title":"","content":"Sorry I just got my book here, can you tell me what page it says merits can only be above 5 dots if you have a power stat above 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T07:40:11-07:00","id":160788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=160786#post160786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry I just got my book here, can you tell me what page it says merits can only be above 5 dots if you have a power stat above 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not say that... nor does it say they can go above 5 at all. See the issue yet?<br /> Vampire provides a RULES precedent for such things. Werewolf does not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> NO WHERE does it say that Totem may exceed 5 Dots except as a Character description (and again, not a rule), in a completely different book entirely. There is NO RULE which allows it explicitly. Character write-ups do not hold the same weight as RULES. I am not arguing that you CAN'T exceed 5 Dots of Totem willy nilly, I am saying that there is a RULES precedent that many tables I have played at follow (no Attribute, Skill, Merit may exceed 5 without a Power stat above 5). And that there are some that do not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-06-2014, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T08:06:58-07:00","id":160808,"title":"","content":"There's also no rule that says you can't have it, though. Your rules precedent is mistaken. Attributes, Skills, and Disciplines can't go above 5 until you meet power stat prereq. It doesn't say anything about merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T08:19:37-07:00","id":160840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155041-totem-creation-help?p=160808#post160808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also no rule that says you can't have it, though. Your rules precedent is mistaken. Attributes, Skills, and Disciplines can't go above 5 until you meet power stat prereq. It doesn't say anything about merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was the case, why would Vampire go out of their way to make exceptions for Characters with Powerstats above 5?<br /> Obviously, because Merits are not intended to exceed 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/